# A creature type that an effect sets replaces the types Changeling gave (CR 205.1b, 613.3; Firdoch Core's ruling: it is
# only that new creature type, and the effect that made it every type is simply overwritten). Oko's +1 makes the Core a
# green 3/3 Elk creature that loses all abilities, so it is no longer an outlaw: Bot2's Shoot the Sheriff, refused for
# the animated Core in firdoch-core-animated-is-an-outlaw-and-keeps-its-own-types, destroys it. Bot1 casts the Core on
# turn 1 (Sol Ring and a Swamp) and Oko on turn 3 (Mox Emerald, Mox Sapphire, Mox Jet).

[Bot1 Deck]
Swamp
Mox Jet
Mox Emerald
Mox Sapphire
Sol Ring
Firdoch Core
Oko, Thief of Crowns
Swamp x12

[Bot2 Deck]
Swamp
Mox Jet
Shoot the Sheriff
Swamp x12

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Swamp.Play
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Sol Ring.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Sol Ring.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Swamp.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Firdoch Core.Cast
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Swamp.Play
Bot2.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Oko, Thief of Crowns.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Oko, Thief of Crowns.Activate(Firdoch Core; Ability: Elk)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Bot1.Battlefield.Firdoch Core.Subtypes = Elk
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Hand.Shoot the Sheriff.Cast(Bot1.Battlefield.Firdoch Core)
Bot2.Battlefield.Swamp.Activate
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate

[Expect]
Bot1.Graveyard = Firdoch Core
